  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ba50969153e34d347a229a276e00ca57, type: 3}
  m_Name: KnownBugsData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::KnownBugsData
  bugs:
  - title: '<Bug> [Crouch]'
    description: When uncrouching under a roof clipping occurs.
  - title: '<Bug> [Unicode] '
    description: 'Having a steam name that uses non english characters can

      break
      the chat, and crash the game.'
  - title: '<Bug> [Settings] '
    description: Resolution Change can make the game Dark.
  - title: '<Bug> [Networking]'
    description: 'After a full session and after win room, when players return to
      Lobby, their state says: In-Elevator.'
  - title: '[Text Chat] White space message keeps the chat open'
    description: 'If you send a whitespace message in the text chat, then chat never
      closes. '
  - title: '[Networking] Player''s names in top right corner don''t reset for reconnected
      client'
    description: When a client reconnects to the Lobby, player names and status in
      the top right corner don't reset.
  - title: '[Collisions] Table Colliders issue & items going through them'
    description: 'Enw exeis ena item, peta to me to x sta podia twn trapeziwn sto
      main room tou game   OBSERVED RESULT  Otan petas ena item se ena trapezi, kanei
      clip mesa apo ta podia tou.   INTENDED RESULT   Ta items prepei na kanoun collide
      me to trapezi  '
  - title: '[Collisions] You should NOT be able to climb on items'
    description: "Me ola ta items boreis na ta kaneis throw kai na aneveis panw tous
      kai ftaseis se merh pou den prepei\n\nOBSERVED RESULT\nO paikths anevainei
      panw sto collider twn items kai mporei na ta xrhsimopoihsei gia na skarfalwsei\n\nINTENDED
      RESULT \nO paikths den mporei na anevei panw sta items "
  - title: '[Collisions] Players should NOT be able to climb on each other'
    description: "Sto multiplayer, oi paiktes mporoun na kanoun stack o enas panw
      ston allo an kapoios einai se mia elevated epifaneia kai mporoun na ftasoun
      inaccessible theseis\n\nOBSERVED RESULT\nO enas paikths kanei stack panw ston
      allo, kai ftanei unintended meroi me to coordination tous. Se afth th periptwsh,
      mporei o enas na paei pisw apo ta rafia kai na kanei softlock olh thn omada
      giati den mporei na figei.\n\nINTENDED RESULT \nOi paiktes prepei na min kanoun
      stack kai na einai teleiws inaccessible gwnies me softlocks san afth sto video"
  - title: '[Elevator] When you spam interact the elevator button, the door animation
      resets'
    description: "Sto multiplayer, an enas paikths kanei spam to interact me to elevator
      button, kanei reset to animation ths portas mexri na stamathsei\n\nOBSERVED
      RESULT\nElevator door animation loops until player stops\n\nINTENDED RESULT
      \nPress the button once, the elevator doors work normally"
  - title: '[Collisions] Main Room Shelf Climbing should NOT happen'
    description: "Se multiplayer kai single player, sto dwmatio akrivws meta apo
      to prwto (pou exei to vending machine) oi paiktes mporoun na:\n\n1) Anaivoun
      sta plevra ths kareklas kai stekontai panw ths\n2)Anevainoun sto pc panw sto
      trapezi\n3)Kanoun aristera kai deksia kai crouch kai anevainoun panw sto rafi\n\nOBSERVED
      RESULT\nPlayers reach an unintended position\n\nINTENDED RESULT \nPlayers cant
      climb over objects and reach these positions"
  - title: '[Collisions] When you walk over props, you can glitch the environment
      and go to places where you shouldn''t'
    description: "\u0391\u03BD \u03C0\u03B5\u03C1\u03C0\u03B1\u03C4\u03AE\u03C3\u03B5\u03B9\u03C2
      \u03C0\u03AC\u03BD\u03C9 \u03C3\u03B5 \u03BC\u03B9\u03BA\u03C1\u03AC objects,
      \u03BF \u03C0\u03B1\u03AF\u03BA\u03C4\u03B7\u03C2 \u03BC\u03C0\u03BF\u03C1\u03B5\u03AF
      \u03BD\u03B1 \u03B1\u03BD\u03AD\u03B2\u03B5\u03B9 \u03C0\u03AC\u03BD\u03C9
      \u03C4\u03BF\u03C5\u03C2 \u03BA\u03B1\u03B9 \u03BC\u03B5\u03C4\u03AC \u03BC\u03C0\u03BF\u03C1\u03B5\u03AF\u03C2
      \u03BD\u03B1 \u03C3\u03BA\u03B1\u03C1\u03C6\u03B1\u03BB\u03CE\u03C3\u03B5\u03B9\u03C2
      \u03C0\u03AC\u03BD\u03C9 \u03C3\u03B5 \u03B1\u03BB\u03BB\u03B1 \u03B1\u03BD\u03C4\u03B9\u03BA\u03B5\u03AF\u03BC\u03B5\u03BD\u03B1"
  - title: '[Networking] PasswordProtectedLobbies - Pressing Join after a wrong password
      will still play join animation'
    description: "\nCurrent Behaviour: Password is wrong but player gets himself
      in the door animation and during the join process and validation the system
      sees his password is wrong and returns him to lobby.\nOn private Lobbies, When
      a player enters a wrong password and presses Join, the door animation still
      plays, and then returns to the menu. \n\nExpected Behaviour : If password is
      wrong just throw an error message on screen and let the player try again without
      puting him in an animation.\n\nRepro:\nA friend needs to already have a private
      lobby hosted, then,\nPlayer 2 presses: \nPlay,\nJoin CoOp\nJoin button next
      to his friends name\nEnter a WRONG password in the input field\nPress the final
      Join button.\n\n\n\nCurrent Behaviour: Password is wrong but player gets himself
      in the door animation and during the join process and validation the system
      sees his password is wrong and returns him to lobby.\nOn private Lobbies, When
      a player enters a wrong password and presses Join, the door animation still
      plays, and then returns to the menu. \n\nExpected Behaviour : If password is
      wrong just throw an error message on screen and let the player try again without
      puting him in an animation.\n\nRepro:\nA friend needs to already have a private
      lobby hosted, then,\nPlayer 2 presses: \nPlay,\nJoin CoOp\nJoin button next
      to his friends name\nEnter a WRONG password in the input field\nPress the final
      Join button.\n\n\n"
  - title: '[Tool - Level Editor] SnapshotID GUIDs reset when viewing prefab in isolation'
    description: After capturing a snapshot of a hierarchy, all its GameObjects will
      have a SnapshotID component with a unique GUID. If that hierarchy is part of
      a prefab, opening the prefab in isolation while also having the prefab loaded
      in a scene will cause the 'scene' instance of the prefab to register overrides
      on every SnapshotID that was loaded twice (once in the scene, and once more
      as the isolated prefab). This causes de-syncs in pre-existing anomalies and
      can lead to data loss.
